I ain't I the luckiest guy in the world  I just found the perfect little helper  what is it with you guys in my family  helping the cops do their job is not  some some privilege it's a trap I'm not  your informant your partner or your  friend the people of Salem are a strange  Bunch  with a serial murderer on the loose the  slow minded citizenry seek safety in a  creepy playground at night and often  alone or maybe they take a cue from the  intrepid individuals currently on a  graveyard tour once again in the dead of  night clearly they do not understand  fear or how sane people would react  during periods of stress murdered soul  suspect is full of these abnormalities  it struggles to frame the supernatural  events in a way that is easily relatable  it's easy to laugh at sole suspect so  why is it so engrossing sole suspects  focus on dissecting people's minds  overshadows its many many missteps  learning the sad details of a girl  murdered by a hooded assailant may be  incredibly uncomfortable  what could possibly compel someone to  commit such a heinous deed the same  sense of unease manifested when I  encountered a ghost who did not realize  that he was dead it assumed his  girlfriend would still come back to him  I cared about the people in Salem even  though so few of them are flushed outs  are more than just caricatures I wanted  to learn their fate are we in for  it's too complicated to get into let's  just say that I wasn't about to let some  judge decide how to spend the rest of my  life that's my choice so I made it  either way no it doesn't matter now does  it  things don't start out too strong Liam  sole suspect you plays ronin a former  criminal who atone for his youthful  errors by joining the police force then  he gets killed by a hooded man and  becomes a ghost hoping to solve the  mystery of his own death he's tough in a  generic distance way that's immediately  off-putting  there's a little more to his personality  than the stoic puffing of a ghostly  cigarettes in the occasional longing for  his deceased ex  Ronin doesn't become more developed even  as you learn more pieces of his life  he's a doll a Parisian who lets his many  tattoos tell a story for him I honestly  didn't even care who finished him off at  any point in the game which seems like a  pretty big problems considering the  entire game is built around solving that  mystery but it's his voyeuristic  tendencies that I found so interesting  as a ghost there's little you can do  aside from snooping on the living you  walk through walls without a care in the  world and survey rooms to find clues  leading you to nebulous answers maybe  you're trying to figure out what caused  a drowned woman to perish while the  other people in the boat were saved or  you're putting together the pieces of a  terrible situation in a police station  there are many ghosts who need your help  in seeing their final moments replayed  kept me pushing forward the most  intriguing of these story threads  belongs to your ex her life was shrouded  in mystery and contradictions that she  was constantly reconciling why does she  trust a former criminal how could  someone with such an open heart have  committed so many felonies and what role  did her own mental instability playing  her decisions gathering these pieces  flushed out her character in ways Ronin  never reaches and provided a stabilizing  presence as I pressed onward the many  faults that surface serve as humorous  diversions rather than sources of  frustration the forced combat sections  that are complete  unnecessary as you vanquish roving  demons the head-scratching stealth  mission that doesn't make any sense  because the medium you're traveling with  was given permission to roam the guarded  premises the goofy cats you inhabit who  you can make me out constantly while  their silly little mouths move  these situations provide levity in a  game that clashes with the serious tone  and even the active exploration is  riddled with problems most of the game  is just walking around discovering clues  to the various stories that exist in  Salem there are so many glitches that  even something as simple as this has  problems for instance items you've  already interacted with remain glowing  they think it seem like there's still  more for you to do or they shimmer as if  they don't exist making you wonder if  it's a bug or just the ethereal plane  messing with you I kept searching  because I loved discovering all these  tidbits even when these problems  surfaced but it still felt shoping  uneven murdered soul suspect is a  strange strange game it does everything  in its power to push you away that is  the taciturn protagonist tired visual  design improper music and brainless  citizens it's empowering to gather the  pieces to the many stories letting you  see the lives of the people play out in  sad detail at least sole suspect has  more spirit than Ronan could ever muster  wrong even when aim is right
 

